description: Persistent checkout and environment onboarding for every Continuum agent
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md and docs/AGENT-START.md at task startup. Establish the actual checkout,
approved task, runtime and database ownership before making changes or running tests.
Preserve dirty work and private files. Follow the existing engineering workflow rule;
chat history does not substitute for verified current source or owner approval.
Read docs/plan/START-HERE.md, docs/plan/CURRENT-PLAN.md and
docs/plan/OWNER-DECISIONS.md. Select dependency-ready work and preserve scoped owner
approvals; do not reopen D01 because an older draft lacks the owner's conversation.
For private local testing context, read the file named by
`git config --get continuum.environmentGuide`. This setting follows linked worktrees,
not fresh clones or cloud agents. Report missing access; never execute the path value.
